@startuml
autonumber
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
title UC-76 - Cancel Paid Order and Request Refund

actor "Guest" as Actor
boundary "Checkout / Payment UI" as FE
control "PaymentController" as API
control "PaymentService" as Service
database "MongoDB: bills, shoesDetail, coupons" as DB
participant "Stripe Gateway" as Stripe_Gateway
participant "Gmail SMTP" as Gmail

Actor -> FE: Trigger use case
API -> Service: Execute Cancel Paid Order and Request Refund
Service -> DB: Read/write bills, shoesDetail, coupons
DB --> Service: Domain data
Service -> Stripe_Gateway: Create/confirm/refund payment
Stripe_Gateway --> Service: Stripe result
Service -> Gmail: Send notification email when configured
Gmail --> Service: Delivery accepted or warning logged
Service --> API: Result
API --> FE: Response
FE --> Actor: Order is CANCELLED and refund is REFUNDED or REFUND_PENDING

alt Alternative / exception flow
  note over FE,Service: Order already SHIPPING or DELIVERED -> cancellation and refund are blocked
  note over FE,Service: Order is not PAID -> cancellation refund is rejected
  note over FE,Service: Stripe refund fails -> system returns error and keeps order unchanged
end

note over Actor,DB
Pre: Order is PAID and fulfillment status is CONFIRMED or PACKING
Post: Order is CANCELLED and refund is REFUNDED or REFUND_PENDING
Main flow:
1. Customer opens order detail from My Orders or guest order lookup
2. System checks order ownership by userId or guest email
3. System verifies payment status is PAID and fulfillment is still being\nprepared
4. Customer enters cancellation reason and confirms Cancel & Refund
5. System calls POST /payments/orders/:orderCode/cancel-refund
6. System restores product stock for cancelled items
7. For Stripe card payment, system creates a Stripe refund from the\nPaymentIntent
8. For bank transfer payment, system marks refund as REFUND_PENDING for\nmanual processing
9. System sets fulfillment status to CANCELLED
10. System sends cancellation and refund email to customer
end note
@enduml
